        <briefdescription>
<para>Checks if the button is hovered by the mouse cursor. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function calculates the normalized position of the mouse cursor relative to the window size, and then checks whether this position falls within the bounds defined by the button&apos;s dimensions. The bounds are calculated as half the width and height of the button, with the center point being at (m_Bounds[0].x, m_Bounds[0].y).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the mouse cursor is hovering over the button, false otherwise.</para>
</simplesect>
Checks if the button is hovered by the mouse cursor.</para>
<para>This function calculates the normalized position of the mouse cursor relative to the framebuffer size, then checks if this position lies within the bounds defined by <computeroutput>m_Bounds</computeroutput>. If it does, the function returns true; otherwise, it returns false.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>A boolean value indicating whether or not the button is hovered by the mouse cursor. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
